From a14257996a5f65db05a94ebb8d3491588cf3186e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Stew Forster <stew675@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 1 Sep 2026 06:50:35 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 13/13] rdna-boosts: block 13: fused MoE gate+up+GLU MMQ + mmvq
 short-K item-split

Fused MoE prefill MMQ kernel (gate+up+GLU triple as one MMQ kernel,
RDNA4-gated, Q3_K/Q4_K/Q5_K/Q8_0/Q6_K) + decode mmvq item-split
((row, kblock) items across thread groups, rpb dispatch 2/4/8) merged
with the upstream has_fusion mmvq path.

Two correctness gates on the try_fuse arms (the fresh 0eadefebd merge
admitted cases the kernels cannot express):
- x_scale_channel_dst fold restricted to single-token MUL_MAT_ID
  (multi-token topk weights are per (expert, token); falls back to the
  separate MUL op, matching the pre-re-base behavior)
- fused MoE MMQ arm gated to the instantiated type list (the other
  mmq_supported types aborted in switch_type_gate)

Includes the GGML_CUDA_OP_TIMING fusion brackets (FUSED op visibility).

Validated on 1-GPU qwen35moe (the verified config): prefill pp16384
Q6_K +5.1%, Q4_K_M +3.6%; decode tg128 +5.6% (97.28 vs 92.15 pristine);
same-seed coherence IDENTICAL; test-backend-ops 2/2 OK.

Assisted-by: Claude Sonnet
